          "const": "update",
          "description": "Update goal metadata. Required args: goal_id. Optional args: title, current_state, description, parent_goal_id, category, goal_kind, value_alignment, pushable. Use update only for an explicit correction that is not already represented by a new activity entry; do not append a generic next step. Use parent_goal_id to move a goal under a new parent; pass empty string to detach to top-level."
        },
        {
          "const": "delete",
          "description": "Delete a goal. Required args: goal_id."
        },
        {
          "const": "add_entry",
          "description": "Add an activity entry to a goal timeline. Required args: goal_id, title, current_state, description. Optional args: effective_at. For every goal type, the runtime replaces the goal's pulse when the activity supports a newer or more useful current or forward-looking status and otherwise preserves it. Do not make a separate update call solely for the runtime's state decision. For assistant-tracked work, log activity incrementally whenever anything happens, including a step starting or completing, a check, new or confirmed information, deliverable progress, an artifact change, a result, checkpoint, check-in, feedback, direction change, blocker, schedule change, or lifecycle change. Do not wait for a milestone or material change. Keep the entry concise and user-facing, say what happened and any result, and record each activity once."
        },
        {
          "const": "edit_entry",
          "description": "Edit an existing goal activity entry. Required args: update_id and at least one of title, current_state, description, effective_at. Keep the entry concise and user-facing, saying what happened and, when applicable, what the result was."
        },
        {
          "const": "delete_entry",
          "description": "Delete an existing goal progress entry. Required args: update_id."
        },
        {
          "const": "set_status",
          "description": "Set the goal lifecycle to active or completed. Required args: goal_id, status, reason. Reason must concisely explain why the lifecycle changed. Use active only to reopen the existing completed goal when the user explicitly restarts the responsibility; never create a replacement goal."
        }
      ],
      "type": "string"
    },
